menu "MiniLoRa"

    config MINILORA_FW_VERSION
        string "Firmware version"
        default "3.0.0"
        help
            Reported in the diagnostics uplink (fport 2) and in the BLE
            advertisement. Bump on every release; the Android app and the
            TTN decoder must stay in sync with the payload contract.

    config MINILORA_GLOBAL_NAME
        string "Default device name (BLE/LoRa)"
        default "MiniLoRa-FX-1"

    config MINILORA_GPS_WARM_ATTEMPTS
        int "GPS warm-start fix budget (seconds)"
        default 240
        range 5 120
        help
            Seconds allotted to the GNSS on wakes from deep sleep (hot/warm
            start when ephemeris and time are retained, TTFF typically 1-10 s;
            after a long indoor spell the module restarts into a cold-ish
            start, TTFF 30-35 s — the budget must cover that). Cold boots
            (power-on) use the full 150 s budget. v1 parity: 60.

    config MINILORA_GPS_BENCH
        bool "GPS bench mode (USB diagnosis, NOT for field use)"
        default n
        help
            Bench/debug builds only: every boot forces a long narrated GPS
            window (min 300 s) regardless of the indoor backoff, and the
            driver counts sentences / checksum failures while the window
            logs satellite counts every 5 s. With battery disconnected and
            USB power this turns the tracker into a live GNSS test bench.
            Never ship with this enabled (no backoff = dead battery fast).

    config MINILORA_BAT_LOW_MV
        int "Low-battery threshold (mV) — degraded mode"
        default 3500
        help
            Below this: no BLE beacon, no Zigbee, sleep interval doubled
            (clamped to 120 min), GPS every other cycle.

    config MINILORA_BAT_CRITICAL_MV
        int "Critical-battery threshold (mV) — survival mode"
        default 3300
        help
            Below this: GPS and sensors off except BME280, only a LoRaWAN
            heartbeat uplink, sleep = 120 min. Config mode (long-press)
            remains available.

    config MINILORA_OTA_CHECK_EVERY
        int "OTA check interval (boots, 0 = disabled)"
        default 96
        help
            Query the MiniLoRa-server for a firmware update every N boots
            (~daily at 15-30 min intervals). Requires the WiFi transport to
            be configured with the server as wifiServerIP:port. An explicit
            OTA_UPDATE remote command bypasses the interval (but never runs
            in critical battery). The device pulls the image over HTTP and
            SHA-256-verifies it before switching boot slots.

endmenu
